1
00:00:03,240 --> 00:00:08,040
Open Artificial Intelligence, File Sources, and click Add File Source.

2
00:00:08,491 --> 00:00:14,661
In Available Connectors, click Add on File system, which reads a folder on the site's server.

3
00:00:15,112 --> 00:00:19,867
Enter a Name, and choose the Target File data source, the one you just made.

4
00:00:19,867 --> 00:00:23,172
Several file sources can feed the same data source.

5
00:00:23,626 --> 00:00:27,493
Keep Enabled ticked, so that the scheduled reading runs.

6
00:00:27,493 --> 00:00:32,046
Re-read interval is how often the folder is read again, in minutes.

7
00:00:32,046 --> 00:00:37,286
The site checks once an hour, so a shorter interval still runs at most hourly.

8
00:00:37,739 --> 00:00:43,096
Figures says whether the charts and pictures inside documents are described:

9
00:00:43,096 --> 00:00:44,599
Auto, All or Off.

10
00:00:44,599 --> 00:00:48,715
Describing figures uses a vision model, so it costs more.

11
00:00:48,715 --> 00:00:51,589
The other fields can stay as they are.

12
00:00:52,042 --> 00:00:56,284
Folder is the folder to read, inside the file sources area that your

13
00:00:56,284 --> 00:00:58,864
technical team set aside for this site.

14
00:00:58,864 --> 00:01:02,532
Tick Include sub-folders to read the folders below it too.

15
00:01:02,986 --> 00:01:04,033
Click Save.

16
00:01:04,033 --> 00:01:09,086
The list shows the source with its connector, and Never run as its last run.

